From c62bd24ff87dc11d2a4132611ad859df987ead99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:03:01 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 43/58] wifi: apple: centauri: Take the bands from the
 firmware's channel list

The driver registered a fixed table: 2.4 GHz channels 1-13 and 25 5 GHz
channels, every one at 20 dBm, and no 6 GHz band. The firmware reports
which channels the current country allows (system command 19), at each
width and with passive and radar flags, and its own capability elements
(system command 8). Before a country is set it reports 2.4 and 5 GHz
only; under US rules it reports 167 entries, 6 GHz channels 1-233 among
them.

- The band plan (2.4 GHz 1-14, 5 GHz 36-177, 6 GHz 1-233) is registered
  once, and the firmware's list is applied over cfg80211's rules: a
  channel it leaves out is disabled, its passive and radar flags become
  NO_IR and RADAR, and a width no entry covers is not used. The power
  limit is left to the regulatory domain and the firmware.
- The regulatory notifier sets the country (command 9, as before), then
  reads the list again and applies it, after every regulatory change.
- 6 GHz is registered with the HE capabilities element the firmware
  reports, and 6 GHz band capabilities from its VHT element; without an
  HE element there is no 6 GHz band. The radio is started before the
  wiphy is registered, since the bands come from it.
- One band encoding, firmware_band(), for scan, connect and beacons. 6 GHz
  beacons carry neither DS parameters nor HT operation, so they take
  their channel from the HE operation's 6 GHz information.
- Scans include the listen-only channels (radar channels, and all of
  6 GHz under US rules) with the firmware's passive and radar bits, as its
  channel list encodes them, instead of skipping them.

Signed-off-by: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>

(cherry picked from commit 855ecf2ad45b0b93555ef4ec1eb69137c059bb63)
[n1-wifi: on aurora-j716s this driver replaces integration's J813/J873 N1 driver files]
